@frenck This is the second issue that I created and that was closed without prior notification because noone replied to it for a month. I remember that previously (e.g. here https://github.com/home-assistant/core/issues/45645) the bot posted a helpful comment before labeling it as stale so you could reply that it's still an issue, thus not letting it be auto-closed a week later.

Is there a reason why this has been changed or a reasonable workaround?

The problem with just labeling it is that I don't get notifications for it, neither by mail nor by the Github app and thus only receive the notification when it already has been closed. But then I can't open it again ;-)
